# Supabase rollout (Engvo)

## Status

- In scope NOW: phases 0–2 + 3-prep only.
- Transport: browser `@supabase/supabase-js` + RLS. No `@supabase/ssr`, middleware, profiles, Realtime, service role in client.
- Out of scope until explicit request: full learning_memory cloud sync, rewards, practice sessions, generated lessons, chat history, OAuth UI, mistakes sync.

## Sequence

0. Infra: browser client, env helpers, feature flags OFF by default
1. Anonymous Auth only (`ensureAnonSession` via `SupabaseBootstrap`)
2. `lesson_progress` local-first sync (metadata + persistent outbox + merge)
3-prep. `learningMemory/record.ts` must use `getLearningMemoryStoragePort()`; local adapter only; no signals tables

## Hard rules

- Do not mirror all localStorage keys into Postgres
- Do not store MyPlan / AttentionZones (derived)
- Do not add SERVICE_ROLE / `sb_secret_*` to client or `NEXT_PUBLIC_*`
- Do not block lesson UX on network; `saveLessonProgress` stays sync `void`
- Do not edit AppShell for bootstrap (UTF-8 risk); use `SupabaseBootstrap`
- Do not enable `NEXT_PUBLIC_FEATURE_SUPABASE_LESSON_PROGRESS_SYNC` before SQL + RLS matrix
- New chats: extend this rollout; do not invent a parallel persistence design
- Domain engvo.ru: Auth redirect URLs later at deploy; not a blocker for 0–2

## Key files

- `lib/supabase/client.ts`, `env.ts`, `ensureAnonSession.ts`
- `components/SupabaseBootstrap.tsx`
- `lib/lessonProgressStorage.ts`, `lib/lessonProgress/*`
- `lib/learningMemory/port.ts`, `record.ts`
- `supabase/migrations/*_lesson_progress.sql`
